$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: To a screw-capped pressure
tube were added anhydrous CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL), aldehyde 3 (0.50 mmol), and
phosphorane 2a (175.0 mg, 0.55 mmol). Then the tube was sealed and heated
to 80 °C until the full consumption of 3 indicated by TLC analysis. The
solvent CH2Cl2 was removed under reduced pressure and then DMF (1.0 mL)
and (R,R)-1 (30.1 mg, 0.05 mmol) were added. The resulting solution was
stirred at -30 °C for half an hour before TMSCN (125 μL, 1.0 mmol) was
charged. After TLC analysis indicated the end of the reaction, the
reaction mixture was poured into NH4Cl (sat.), after usual work-up
procedure and column chromatography using PE/Et2O (10:0 to10:1) as the
eluent could afford the corresponding products 5. The reaction with 3a
was conducted for 12 hours for step 1 and 3 days for step 2; Column
chromatography afforded 5a in 71% yield as colorless oil.26 The reaction
with 3b was conducted for 19 hours for step 1 and 2 days for step 2;
Column chromatography afforded 5b in 75% yield as colorless oil. The
isomeric composition of the product: 93% ee. Chiral GC analysis [Agilent,
Chirasil DEX CB 25 m × 0.25 mm × 0.25 μm, column temp = 90 °C, Injector
temp = 200 °C, Detector temp = 250 °C, Inlet pressure = 75 kPa), tr
(major) = 24.07 min, tr (minor) = 23.66 min.]. [α]D 25 = -0.7 (c = 0.90,
CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.02-5.95 (m, 1H), 5.46 (dt, J = 15.6,
1.2 Hz, 1H), 2.00-1.94 (m, 2H), 1.74-1.66 (m, 1H), 1.63 (s, 3H),
0.92-0.89 (m, 6H), 0.21 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 131.96,
131.60, 121.15, 69.89, 41.14, 31.09, 28.18, 22.50, 22.32, 1.48; IR (KBr)
ν 2958.8, 2359.7, 2342.0, 1254.0, 1111.9, 1001.6, 973.6, 757.1, 668.9
cm-1; MS (EI): 225 (M+, 0.78), 183 (11), 154 (100), 127 (87), 129 (55),
75 (69), 73 (40), 55 (23); HRMS (EI): Exact mass calcd for C12H23NOSi:
225.1549, found: 225.1551.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 93% ee, sealed tube used, Wittig reaction (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Activation of chiral (Salen)AlCl complex by phosphorane for highly
enantioselective cyanosilylation of ketones and enones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zeng, Xing-Ping; Cao, Zhong-Yan; Wang, Xin; Chen, Long; Zhou, Feng; Zhu,
Feng; Wang, Cui-Hong; Zhou, Jian
