$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure: To a screw-capped pressure tube were added anhydrous
CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL), aldehyde 3 (0.50 mmol), and phosphorane 2a (175.0 mg,
0.55 mmol). Then the tube was sealed and heated to 80 °C until the full
consumption of 3 indicated by TLC analysis. The solvent CH2Cl2 was
removed under reduced pressure and then DMF (1.0 mL) and (R,R)-1 (30.1
mg, 0.05 mmol) were added. The resulting solution was stirred at -30 °C
for half an hour before TMSCN (125 μL, 1.0 mmol) was charged. After TLC
analysis indicated the end of the reaction, the reaction mixture was
poured into NH4Cl (sat.), after usual work-up procedure and column
chromatography using PE/Et2O (10:0 to10:1) as the eluent could afford the
corresponding products 5. The reaction with 3a was conducted for 12 hours
for step 1 and 3 days for step 2; Column chromatography afforded 5a in
71% yield as colorless oil.26 The isomeric composition of the product:
90% ee. HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OJ-H+OJ-H, i PrOH/hexane = 3/97, 1.0
mL/min, 205 nm; tr (major) = 16.92 min, tr (minor) = 18.78 min). [α]D 25
= -10.0 (c = 1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.38-7.28 (m, 5H),
6.11 (dt, J = 15.5, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 5.79 (dt, J = 15.5, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 4.55
(s, 2H), 4.07 (dd, J = 5.0, 1.6 Hz, 2H), 1.66 (s, 3H), 0.23 (s, 9H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 137.99, 132.32, 128.55, 127.86, 127.77, 120.80,
72.75, 69.49, 68.99, 30.69, 1.46.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, 90% ee, sealed tube used,
Wittig reaction (stage 1)
