$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: To a screw-capped pressure
tube were added anhydrous CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL), α,β-unsaturated enal 10 (0.5
mmol), and phosphorane 2 (175.0 mg, 0.55 mmol). Then the tube was sealed
and heated to 80 °C until the full consumption of 10 indicated by TLC
analysis. After the reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature (rt),
(salen)AlCl (R,R)-1 (30.3 mg, 0.05 mmol) was added. The resulting
solution was cooled to -30 or -40 °C (as indicated above) and stirred for
half an hour before the addition of TMSCN (1.0 mmol). After TLC analysis
indicated the full conversion of the trans-6 (cis-6 was unreactive in
step 2 in most cases), the mixture was directly subjected for column
chromatograph, and product 7 was isolated using petroleum ether/diethyl
ether (from 100:0 to 10:1) as the eluent. The reaction with 10a was
conducted for 25 hours for step 1 and 2 days for step 2 at -30 °C; Column
chromatography afforded 7a in 70% yield as pale yellow oil. The reaction
with 10b was conducted for 25 hours for step 1 and 2 days for step 2 at
-30 °C; Column chromatography afforded 7b in 71% yield as pale yellow
oil. The isomeric composition of the product: 92% ee. HPLC analysis
(Chiralcel OJ-H+OJ-H, i PrOH/hexane = 1/99, 0.8 mL/min, 230 nm; tr(major)
= 28.35 min, tr(minor) = 31.67 min). [α]D 25 = -30.0 (c = 1.0, CHCl3); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.26-7.22 (m, 3H), 7.08 (s, 1H), 6.75-6.63 (m,
3H), 5.73 (d, J = 15.2 Hz, 1H), 2.36 (s, 3H), 1.70 (s, 3H), 0.24 (s, 9H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 138.34, 136.57, 135.81, 132.71, 131.52,
129.09, 128.67, 127.39, 126.28, 123.88, 120.80, 69.78, 30.88, 21.46,
1.48; IR (ATR) ν 2959.3, 1641.8, 1253.1, 1195.5, 1099.7, 988.1, 842.2,
756.0, 690.8 cm-1; MS (EI): 285 (M+, 61), 270 (77), 242 (51), 196 (29),
172 (97), 143 (76), 128 (36), 73 (100). HRMS (EI): Exact mass calcd for
C17H23NOSi: 285.1549; found: 285.1553.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 92% ee, sealed tube used, Wittig reaction (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Activation of chiral (Salen)AlCl complex by phosphorane for highly
enantioselective cyanosilylation of ketones and enones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zeng, Xing-Ping; Cao, Zhong-Yan; Wang, Xin; Chen, Long; Zhou, Feng; Zhu,
Feng; Wang, Cui-Hong; Zhou, Jian
