$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure: To a screw-capped pressure tube were added anhydrous
CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL), α,β-unsaturated enal 10 (0.5 mmol), and phosphorane 2
(175.0 mg, 0.55 mmol). Then the tube was sealed and heated to 80 °C until
the full consumption of 10 indicated by TLC analysis. After the reaction
mixture was cooled to room temperature (rt), (salen)AlCl (R,R)-1 (30.3
mg, 0.05 mmol) was added. The resulting solution was cooled to -30 or -40
°C (as indicated above) and stirred for half an hour before the addition
of TMSCN (1.0 mmol). After TLC analysis indicated the full conversion of
the trans-6 (cis-6 was unreactive in step 2 in most cases), the mixture
was directly subjected for column chromatograph, and product 7 was
isolated using petroleum ether/diethyl ether (from 100:0 to 10:1) as the
eluent. The reaction with 10a was conducted for 25 hours for step 1 and 2
days for step 2 at -30 °C; Column chromatography afforded 7a in 70% yield
as pale yellow oil. The isomeric composition of the product: 91% ee. HPLC
analysis (Chiralcel OJ-H, i PrOH/hexane = 1/99, 1.0 mL/min, 230 nm; tr
(major) = 16.67 min, tr (minor) = 13.64 min). [α]D 25 = -31.2 (c = 1.0,
CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.43-7.41 (m, 2H), 7.34 (t, J = 8.0
Hz, 2H), 7.28-7.24 (m, 1H), 6.75-6.64 (m, 3H), 5.74 (d, J = 14.8 Hz, 1H),
1.70 (s, 3H), 0.24 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 136.66, 135.68,
132.96, 131.43, 128.79, 128.27, 126.71, 126.49, 120.80, 69.76, 30.90,
1.49; IR (ATR) ν 3027.45, 2959.79, 1642.71, 1490.92, 1253.12, 1099.57,
989.31, 842.06, 747.14, 690.40 cm-1; MS (EI): 271 (M+, 58), 256 (66), 228
(62), 182 (24), 157 (100), 129 (51), 115 (21), 73 (92). HRMS (EI): Exact
mass calcd for C16H21NOSi: 271.1392; found: 271.1394.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, 91% ee, sealed tube used,
Wittig reaction (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Activation of chiral (Salen)AlCl complex by phosphorane for highly
enantioselective cyanosilylation of ketones and enones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zeng, Xing-Ping; Cao, Zhong-Yan; Wang, Xin; Chen, Long; Zhou, Feng; Zhu,
Feng; Wang, Cui-Hong; Zhou, Jian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2016), 138(1), 416-425

